id: 14
hanzi: 彼此
pinyin: bǐ cǐ
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Pronoun

meanings_summary:
  en: each other; one another; mutually; both parties; (polite) the same to you
  es: el uno al otro; mutuamente; entrambos; ambas partes; (cortesía) igualmente

senses[2]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Pronoun | Standard | each other; one another; referring to both sides or parties in a mutual reciprocal relationship | el uno al otro; recíprocamente; ambas partes en una relación de reciprocidad | 彼此信任 (trust each other)
  2 | Pronoun | Colloquial | polite formulaic reply returning praise or greeting ('likewise / the same to you / we are both in the same boat') | respuesta cortés de cortesía ('igualmente / estamos en las mismas / mutuo') | 彼此彼此 (likewise / same to you)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 经过漫长时间的朝夕相伴，老人与猴群彼此建立起了无需语言翻译的深厚心灵默契。 | Jīngguò màncháng shíjiān de zhāoxī-xiāngbàn, lǎorén yǔ hóuqún bǐcǐ jiànlì qǐ le wúxū yǔyán fānyì de shēnhòu xīnlíng mòqì. | Through long days and nights together, the elder and the monkey troop built tacit mutual rapport requiring no linguistic translation. | A través de una prolongada convivencia diaria, el anciano y la manada forjaron una honda compenetración mutua que prescindía de palabras.
  #2 | 面对全球性气候危机的共同考验，世界各国应当放下地缘政治分歧，在彼此尊重的基础上深化互利合作。 | Miànduì quánqiúxìng qìhòu wēijī de gòngtóng kǎoyàn, shìjiè gèguó yīngdāng fàngxià dìyuán-zhèngzhì fēnqí, zài bǐcǐ zūnzhòng de jīchǔ shàng shēnhuà hùlì hézuò. | Facing the common test of climate crises, nations should set aside geopolitics and deepen cooperation on mutual respect. | Ante el reto común de la crisis climática, los países deben aparcar discrepancias geopolíticas y ahondar su cooperación sobre el respeto mutuo.

collocations[6]{hanzi,en}:
  彼此信任 | trust one another mutually
  彼此尊重 | mutual respect
  彼此理解 | mutual understanding
  彼此关照 | take care of each other
  彼此彼此 | same to you; likewise (polite formula)
  拉近彼此距离 | shorten the distance between each other

idioms[4]{hanzi,pinyin,meaning_en}:
  彼此彼此 | bǐ cǐ bǐ cǐ | likewise; same to both of us; in the same boat
  顾此失彼 | gù cǐ shī bǐ | attend to one and lose the other; unable to attend to both
  厚此薄彼 | hòu cǐ bó bǐ | favor one over the other; treat with discrimination
  不分彼此 | bù fēn bǐ cǐ | make no distinction between what is yours and mine; share intimately

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  彼 | bǐ | that; there; the other; those | aquel; ese; el otro; aquello | 彳 | step / walk | 彳 (walking along the road) | 皮 (pí, animal hide / phonetic) | 8 | 左右结构 | Phono-semantic compound: step radical 彳 indicating walking into the distance, paired with 皮. Means 'that distant other'. | Taking measured footsteps along the road (彳) toward that distant, far-off horizon points toward the other (彼). | Avanzar con pasos medidos (彳) hacia el horizonte distante señala aquello lejano y al otro (彼). | 214 | HODHE | 
  此 | cǐ | this; here; present | este; esta; esto; aquí; presente | 止 | stop / foot | 止 (foot planted on the ground) | 匕 (bǐ, sitting person close by) | 6 | 左右结构 | Ancient oracle bone pictogram of a person 匕 standing with foot 止 firmly planted right here on the ground, meaning 'this place / here'. | A person pauses and plants their foot firmly on the earth (止) right here in this present spot (此). | Una persona planta con firmeza la planta del pie (止) justo en este lugar y en este instante (此). | 214 | YMP | 

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Linking what is situated far over there (彼) with what is planted right here (此) encompasses both parties and each other (彼此).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Conectar lo que está allá a lo lejos (彼) con lo que reposa aquí a los pies (此) abarca a ambas partes el uno con el otro (彼此).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: In ancient classical grammar, 彼 (that / the other) and 此 (this / oneself) formed a spatial deictic binary. Fused together, 彼此 transcended polar opposition into a reciprocal relational pronoun uniting two parties in intersubjective dialogue.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Dual dipping 3rd tones: 'bǐ cǐ'. Under standard Mandarin sandhi, the first 3rd tone shifts to rising 2nd tone: 'bí cǐ' (35-214).

